  "turns": [
    {
      "id": "t1",
      "instruction": "Analyze the attached 18 m symmetric double-slope trapezoidal truss in the global X-Z plane. The horizontal bottom chord has six 3 m panels: B0 through B6 at x=0,3,6,9,12,15,18 m and z=0. Top nodes T0 through T6 have the same x coordinates and z=1.6,1.9,2.2,2.5,2.2,1.9,1.6 m. The top slope is +1/10 from x=0 to 9 m and -1/10 from x=9 to 18 m. Connect adjacent nodes along each chord, add all seven verticals Bi-Ti including both end verticals, and add exactly T0-B1, T1-B2, T2-B3, T3-B4, T4-B5 and T5-B6 as web diagonals. Use the full 25-member endpoint table and axial-only, pin-jointed rods. B0 is a pin; B6 is a bilateral vertical roller free in global X. Case D applies 15 kN downward (global -Z) only at each of B1 through B5. Use the supplied material and area records and run first-order linear static analysis in OpenSees with self-weight disabled. Report signed ux and uz of all five loaded bottom nodes, signed N for every bottom-chord, top-chord and web member, and Fx/Fz reactions at both supports. N is positive in tension. Identify D, node/member IDs and units for every output.\n\nUse the complete attached input tables. Global XYZ is right handed with Z upward; any planar model uses the XZ plane. All nodes listed are connected physical joints. Member local x points from i to j. In 2D local y=global +Y and local z=x cross y. In 3D local y=normalize(reference cross x), local z=x cross y; reference vectors are explicit. N is positive in tension. Signed section N/T/M2/M3 equal minus the i-end resisting action at the start and plus the j-end action at the end; V2/V3 use plus i-end and minus j-end action. Report global nodal displacements and support reactions; rotations follow the right-hand rule. Distributed loads act per actual member length, including inclined members. Use first-order linear elasticity with self-weight, rigid floors, rigid offsets, P-delta and construction stages off. Use only the specified cases and combinations. Compute every request in output-requests.json, retaining its location, side, signed component, unit and case/combination. Interior forces must include applied-load terms. Execute OpenSees and retain version, runnable input, current-model hash, run ID, actual solver log and raw result/case mapping. Report the requested results in the response body as well as structured results; independently check equilibrium. No numerical answer or native execution evidence is supplied.",
      "state": 1,
      "expectation": "analyze",
      "attachments": [
        "geometry.json",
        "properties.json",
        "loads.json",
        "output-requests.json"
      ],
      "unresolvedFields": [],
      "expectedQuestions": []
    }
  ],
